{"kind":"event","event_id":5254,"event_uid":"01M2M1QBJPFKA0VRQMXWW3XBPP","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":243,"issue_uid":"01M2M1N02552BPP06QYWG29Y2Q","issue_short_id":"9y2q","actor":"impl:1@run-153","hlc_physical_ms":1789526781526,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"fc31ab66da15d4fe9473fc2d9f98070ebd68ef3be860f2c48e4b90bab1c9a358","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2M1QBJMC68X8YC20HP3SBZN","author":"impl:1@run-153","body":"Task 1 approach: move the prompt off argv onto the child's stdin in fleet/run-worker.mjs runProcess — spawn [cli, ['-p'].concat(argv)] with stdio ['pipe','pipe','pipe'], attach child.stdin.on('error', () => {}) before child.stdin.end(prompt) so an EPIPE from a child that exits before reading cannot become an uncaught exception. Rewrite the two comment blocks (above buildArgs, above runProcess) to say what is now true, and change the evidence 'cmd' line to 'claude -p … (prompt on stdin)' keeping the prompt body below the '--- prompt ---' marker. Give test_worker_kata_env.mjs's spawnFn stub a stdin with on/end. Write fleet/tests/test_worker_prompt_stdin.mjs to the four legs the Proof names (a 200k-byte multi-byte prompt byte-compared at stdin, argv element size/'-p'/no-prompt-prefix, an EPIPE-after-close dispatch that still resolves, and the kata-env sentinel).","created_at":"2026-09-16T02:46:21.524995584Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T02:46:21.526Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":5255,"event_uid":"01M2M1QTBYVHNNMZQXPJHH8S4F","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":244,"issue_uid":"01M2M1N3WNZQQVDFKX12F2ESCS","issue_short_id":"escs","actor":"impl:2@run-153","hlc_physical_ms":1789526796670,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"619bed1b98190d293a27d4ab060603a5952bd34c59b6a025b6ab7c0a181fee3f","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2M1QTBXN471H80CKMQ8GJ13","author":"impl:2@run-153","body":"Task 2 approach: (1) resolveConflicts takes contendingBlock as string | (conflict)=>string, resolved with one expression at the agent() call; (2) new export writeResolverBriefs in fleet/publish-fold.mjs writes <briefsDir>/contending-<i>-<attemptKey>.txt per open conflict and copies mainPatch to <briefsDir>/main.patch, returning the per-conflict two-line pointer string; (3) publish-fold step 4 uses briefsDir = <runDir>/publish-fold/briefs (inside the resolver's --add-dir) and copies each contending file into foldEvidence for the record; (4) resolver.md gains one paragraph naming the two lines, CONTRACT.md's publish-fold receipts list gains contending-<i>-<attempt>.txt.","created_at":"2026-09-16T02:46:36.669582885Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T02:46:36.67Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":5256,"event_uid":"01M2M1T8BGP2BSW2D80EH1T2RA","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":244,"issue_uid":"01M2M1N3WNZQQVDFKX12F2ESCS","issue_short_id":"escs","actor":"exam:2@run-153","hlc_physical_ms":1789526876528,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"24863fe3b8c97a997daee11dee5231438ffa6c713a091cad0a896f5118d6afcc","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2M1T8BF2CY9QSQ8K248A7NE","author":"exam:2@run-153","body":"exam (task 2, `fleet/tests/test_resolver_brief.mjs`): writing the sim as plain `node:assert/strict` + a closing `ALL TESTS PASSED` line, the shape every sibling under `fleet/tests/` uses.\n\nReadings I am pinning, so a later session does not re-derive them:\n\n- **M1/M2 rig.** `resolveConflicts` is imported by name from `../run-engine.mjs` (it exists at BASE). The two-conflict stop drains exactly as the task's Context says: the first `resolve` answers `{applied:true, waiting:[2]}`, which passes the engine's `expectWaiting` check (`outstanding.slice(1).map(e=>e.i)` === `[2]`) and shifts to conflict 2; the second answers `{applied:true, complete:true, selfChecks:'ok'}`. So the fake `agent` records exactly two prompts, in `open` order, and legs (a)/(b) can index them.\n- **M3 import shape.** `writeResolverBriefs` is read through a *namespace* import (`import * as publishFold from '../publish-fold.mjs'`) plus an explicit `typeof === 'function'` assertion, not a named import. A named import of an absent export is an ESM link error that kills the file before any leg reports; the namespace form lets BASE fail on the leg that is actually absent.\n- **M3 `blockFor` arity.** The exam's `blockFor` is synchronous and returns a string. The real call site (`buildContendingBlock`) is async, so an implementation will likely `await` it — awaiting a plain string is fine either way. A synchronous fake is the permissive choice and does not pin the implementation to one of the two.\n- **Leg (c) matching.** The leg says the returned string 'has a line starting `CONTENDING TASKS FILE: ` + that absolute path', so the assertion is `startsWith` on that prefix, not equality with the whole line — the trailing parenthetical the Context sketches is Context, not a Machine clause, and pinning it would grade one particular wording.\n- **Legs (d)/(e).** The Proof routes these to its `Run:` grep lines, but they are also encoded inside the sim (reading `../roles/resolver.md` and `../CONTRACT.md` relative to the file's landing directory) so every leg earns an assertion in the exam itself. The word count is `console.log`ged and gates nothing, per leg (e). The global constraint's stylistic pin (no all-caps `MUST`/`NEVER`/`ALWAYS`/`DO NOT`) is asserted too; it is green at BASE and stays green for any implementation that keeps the file's register.\n\nExpected at BASE: red on leg (a) — the engine concatenates `contendingBlock` as a value, so a function stringifies into the brief.","created_at":"2026-09-16T02:47:56.527142927Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T02:47:56.528Z"}
